cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Sign and Countersign: Cryptographic Identity Is Necessary but Not Sufficient for Agent Swarms"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered testbed that measures which attacks on agent-to-agent messaging
  each layer of identity defence stops (no defence, a shared TOTP handshake,
  per-agent Ed25519 signatures, and signatures plus an external reference monitor),
  with attack success read from a fake payment ledger. Apart Research Swarm Alignment Sprint (November 2026),
  Track 3 (Strengthening Agent Infrastructure).
authors:
  - family-names: Uzoatu
    given-names: Ifeanyi Bryan
    affiliation: "University of Bristol"
repository-code: "https://github.com/U-Bryan/sign-countersign"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-07"
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - multi-agent systems
  - agent-to-agent protocols
  - prompt injection
  - authentication
  - reference monitor
